<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahluwalia misl</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ahluwalia misl was one of the twelve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-confederacy">Sikh confederacies</a> of 18th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jassa-singh-ahluwalia">Jassa Singh Ahluwalia</a>, who also commanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-khalsa">Dal Khalsa</a>. It held lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bist-doab">Jalandhar Doab</a> and took Kapurthala in the 1770s. Unlike most misls, it survived the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>, and its chiefs ruled the princely state of Kapurthala until 1947.</p></div>
